@wscunningham captured this incredible light pillar in Colorado while driving back from the CalWood burn zone, and it looks just like a portal to another dimension.⁠
⁠
Light pillars form when light reflects off tiny, flat ice crystals floating in freezing air. The crystals stretch the light into a glowing vertical column, which makes it look like a beam suspended in mid-air.

The Harvest Moon, glowing red over Bali 🌕❤️⁠
⁠
@manusianlangit captured the full moon closest to the autumn equinox, known as the Harvest Moon. When it sits low on the horizon, Earth’s atmosphere filters its light, giving it this warm, fiery glow.
